# Branch and PR lifecycle

Agents must **check git and memory palace** before starting non-trivial work and
**propose** branch/PR actions to Warren (do not merge to `main` without explicit
"promote to main" / "merge to main" / "merge the PR").

## Read before proposing

1. `docs/memory/CURRENT.md` — branch, PR, blockers, next steps
2. `git status`, `git branch --show-current`, `git log origin/main..HEAD --oneline`
3. `docs/BACKLOG.md` — only entries whose **TRIGGER** fired for the next task
4. Open PRs (`gh pr list` or GitHub) for the current branch

## Suggest **merge PR → main** when ALL apply

- User explicitly asks to merge/promote, **or**
- Current feature branch work is **complete** for a coherent unit (tests/lint
  passing or failures reported separately)
- `CURRENT.md` "next" items are **different theme** than what shipped (e.g.
  memory/docs done → next is Celery queue split)
- Branch has been open **>1 week** or **>15 commits** ahead of `main` without merge
- No uncommitted work that belongs in the same PR (commit or stash first)

**Proposal format:** PR number, title, summary bullets, test plan gaps, then:
"Recommend merging PR #N, then branch `feat/...` for &lt;next TRIGGER&gt;."

## Suggest **new branch** when ANY apply

- After merge to `main`: always `git checkout main && git pull` then
  `git checkout -b feat/<short-topic>`
- Next task is a **different TRIGGER** or capability area (import parity vs infra
  vs commercial planner)
- Current branch name no longer matches work (e.g. steward perf done, starting
  topology work)
- Dirty tree mixes unrelated concerns → split via new branch after commit on
  current branch

**Branch naming:** `feat/`, `fix/`, or `docs/` + kebab-case topic; not
`cursor/cloud-agent-*` on local desktop unless cloud handoff.

## Suggest **stay on current branch** when

- Same TRIGGER / same importer / same incident in progress
- PR not yet merged but next commit is clearly part of the same deliverable
- User said "continue on this branch"

## After merge (agent checklist)

1. Merge PR (or user merges); `git checkout main && git pull origin main`
2. Update `CURRENT.md`: branch `main`, note merge commit, clear "open PR"
3. Append `CONTEXT.md` changelog line
4. Create new feature branch for next work; set `CURRENT.md` branch field
5. `Run cip-git-handoff` if switching local ↔ cloud

## Never

- Force-push `main`
- Merge with unexplained dirty tree (untracked smoke DB, beat schedule files)
- Open a second PR for the same branch without closing/superseding the first
